    "result_text": "Done. The build is green.\n\nI implemented the city-capacity rule by adding small, cohesive new units and touching only one existing file (the POST pipeline YAML), keeping structural impact minimal:\n\n- **`EnsureCityCapacity`** (new function) \u2014 counts existing owners whose city matches (case-insensitive) and throws when the count is \u2265 50, before the owner is saved.\n- **`CityAtCapacityException`** (new checked exception) \u2014 carries the city and count into the message.\n- **`CityAtCapacityExceptionHandler`** (new escalation handler) \u2014 responds `409 Conflict` with a `ProblemDetail`, mirroring the existing duplicate handlers.\n- **Escalation YAML** wiring the exception to its handler.\n- One edit to `owners.POST.yml`: inserted the `ensureCityCapacity` step between `countNamesakes` and `save`.\n\nEach new function has essentially no surrounding class complexity, and I didn't grow any existing method. `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` and the full suite pass.",
